			"notes": "- Radio-Kinetic Transceiver improvements:\n    - Receiver units no longer cost additional stress by default\n    - Receiver units can be configured to no cost, flat cost, or cost per RPM\n    - Transceivers no longer have an output stress capacity limit per RPM by default\n    - Limit can be turned on in config and accepts a multiplier value\n    - Transmitter units connection range now scales with RPM\n    - Added range per RPM can be configured, default 1.5 blocks per RPM\n    - Added a visual indicator for range (toggleable with keybind) shown while making connections with cable item\n    - General optimizations\n- Clipboard copy/paste capability for Bus blocks\n- Fixed a bug that cause servers to be unable to load/start due to advancement issue (Issue #27)\n- Fixed a bug that caused clipboard pastes on Hub blocks to ignore Dashpanels module locations\n\nDecided against reducing the stress cost for a Radio-Kinetic Transmitter unit from 2.0x RPM to 1.0x RPM. With stress cost at 2.0x RPM both sizes of waterwheel are invalid ways to transmit stress over large distances at any speed (unless they are chained). This was kept for balancing reasons."
		},
